A||||3||Cliff Pennock||Battery Connectors - keep 'm clean!||||4
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||09-13-1999||06:02 PM||||Just a small "Duh!"-tip:<P>Some electrical problems can easily be caused by a loose or oxidated battery connector. If the battery cable doesn't make full contact with the battery, then the battery can not deliver it's full current. You might not notice it until you have several things turned on at once in your car like lights, windshield-wipers, A/C or heater etc. The connection fails because to much current is trying to flow through a small connection causing the metal to actually melt and make things worse (molten metal hardly conducts).<P>The reason for this "Duh"-tip? I almost had my car towed today because it wouldn't start. Everything worked until I turned the ignition. Turned out the battery cable's connector needed some cleaning...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 09-13-1999).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Harry||09-13-1999||09:16 PM||||Being a squid the Navy has taught me a very good lesson in preventative maintenance.<BR>I make it a habit the first weekend of every month to clean my Post's and clamps.<BR>Always good to never be caught with a dirty post.<BR>Could mess up a really good day!||||reg||6
